    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever tasted "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bubble",
            "ref": "v-bubble"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " tea? This sweet and tasty drink is as fun as it sounds."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "☺ The “bubble” isn’t what you think it is."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Most people think that the word “bubble” in bubble tea "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "refers to",
            "ref": "v-refer-to"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the little "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tapioca",
            "zh": "木薯淀粉"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " balls at the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "bottom",
            "zh": "底部"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of the cup. But that’s not true! The “bubble” refers to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "foam",
            "ref": "v-foam"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on the top of the tea. This comes from when people shake ice, milk, tea and sugar together. The drink was named for it."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "☺ A "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "bored",
            "ref": "v-bored"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " woman in a meeting first made the tea."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In 1988, a woman named "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Lin Hsiu Hui",
            "zh": "林秀慧"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " worked in the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Chun Shui Tang",
            "zh": "春水堂"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " teahouse in Taiwan, China. She was feeling "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "a bit",
            "zh": "有点儿"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " bored in a meeting one day. So she "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "dumped",
            "zh": "倾倒"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a Chinese dessert from Taiwan, China called “fen yuan” into her "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "iced",
            "ref": "v-iced"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " tea. She drank it and it was "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "delicious",
            "ref": "v-delicious"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "! It was so yummy that it quickly became a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "top-selling",
            "zh": "最畅销的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " drink."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "☺ Bubble tea is one of its many different names."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A drink of many names, bubble tea is often called "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "boba",
            "zh": "波霸"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " tea, pearl tea or milk tea. It is also known as "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "pearl",
            "ref": "v-pearl"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " shake, tapioca milk tea, QQ and many other names. Call it what you like and enjoy. But don’t drink too much of it!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "n1",
        "type": "note",
        "title": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Did you know?"
          }
        ],
        "content": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "中国台湾甜点“（珍珠）粉圆”，是一种由木薯粉制成，外观晶莹剔透，口感润滑有弹性的可口点心。"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
